      <abstract>
        <sec>
          <title>Background</title>
          <p>Egg weight (EW) is a key trait with heritability <inline-formula><mml:math id="M1"><mml:msup><mml:mi>h</mml:mi><mml:mn>2</mml:mn></mml:msup></mml:math></inline-formula> reported between 0.4 and 0.6.</p>
        </sec>
        <sec>
          <title>Results</title>
          <p>Using 12,000 SNPs we estimated <italic>h</italic><sup>2</sup> = 0.45.</p>
        </sec>
        <sec>
          <title>Conclusions</title>
          <p>Genomic selection for EW is feasible.</p>
        </sec>
      </abstract>
